==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*meh₂d-|id=wet}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|NL.|mastoīdēs}}, from {{bor|en|grc|μᾰστοειδής||like a breast}}, from {{af|grc|μᾰστός|-ειδής|t1=a woman's breast|t2=-like, -oid|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmæ.stɔɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-mastoid.wav|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|æstɔɪd|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Being the [[process]] of the [[temporal bone]] behind the [[ear]].
## {{lb|en|zootomy}} Being any of several [[bony]] elements that occupy a similar position in the [[skull]] of lower [[vertebrate]]s.
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Of or relating to the [[mastoid process]] of the [[temporal bone]].
# {{lb|en|botany}} Shaped like a [[nipple]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1899|title=Memoirs of the Torrey Botanical Club|volume=6-8|page=192
|passage=Spores tetrahedral, paraphyses '''mastoid'''-claviform, scales smooth, entire.}}

